#version 460
// d4r engine, preset L: the input stage (KIND 3, rrlite_enc0_4x4_*) and the expansion stage (KIND 4, rrlite_dec0_4x4)
// for GPUs without cooperative matrices or FP8 (RDNA2). The mathematics, parameters and bindings are layer_m.comp's
// KIND 3 and 4 (L_NOTES.md) in its relaxed build; the products and number formats are layer_m_dot2.comp's (v_dot4_i32_i8
// on int8 with per-token and per-column scales, v_dot2_f32_f16 on exact FP8 values in binary16), on the matrices
// runtime_m.inc widenM packs for preset L. The input stage's patch merge is merge_l_dot2.comp, dispatched after it.
//  - A workgroup is one 8x8-pixel block, two waves: a lane owns one pixel's token (window-major, so a half-wave holds one
//    4x4-pixel window) with all its 32 channels. The norms, the int8 scales, the embedding and the MLP's hidden values
//    therefore stay in the lane's registers: no shared memory or barrier but the expansion stage's patch expand
//    (layer_m_dot2.comp splits a token's channels across waves; at C 32 its exchanges cost more than its products).
//  - Weights are wave-uniform (scalar memory). Attention as layer_m_dot2.comp: a window's keys come as DPP8
//    broadcasts within groups of eight lanes and a swap of the two groups.
